-- title:
--   Maximal ideal of the crossing model W[[u,v]]/(uv-π)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative local ring and let $\pi \in W$ be a non-unit, i.e. $\pi$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$. Write $M =$ `UVCrossingModel W π` for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W \cong W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \pi$ (the constant power series attached to $\pi$), and assume that $M$ is itself local. Let `UVCrossingModel.constHom π : W →+* M` be the ring homomorphism sending $w$ to the class of the constant power series $w$, and let `U π` and `V π` denote the classes in $M$ of the variables $X_0$ and $X_1$. The assertion is that the maximal ideal of $M$ equals the supremum (sum) of two ideals: the ideal of $M$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $W$ under `UVCrossingModel.constHom π`, and the ideal generated by the two elements `U π` and `V π`. In classical notation, $\mathfrak m_M = \mathfrak m_W M + (u,v)$.
--
--   This identifies the maximal ideal of the standard crossing (node) model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ over a local base in which $\pi$ is not invertible, without assuming the maximal ideal of $W$ to be principal. It is used in the local analysis of nodal points on modular and other curves, for instance in the computations of lengths and of ranks of quotients by the ideals cut out at a node, and in the pullback description of completed local rings at a crossing.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_maximalIdeal_eq_map_maximalIdeal_sup_span_pair.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
